ANZAC_Peace_Park_1.JPG/960px-ANZAC_Peace_Park_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Alison Hartman Gardens","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.02271,"lo":117.8829,"d":809,"ds":"Alison Hartman Garden, often referred to as Mokare Park, is a park on York Street in Albany in the Great Southern region of Western Australia. The park, located near the centre of Albany, contains numerous sculptures including the statue of Mokare. The area is situated adjacent to the Albany Public Library and the Albany Town Square.","wpu":"Alison Hartman Gardens","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/AHG2.jpg/960px-AHG2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Port Albany, Western Australia","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.03092,"lo":117.90032,"d":1080,"ds":"Port Albany is a suburb of the City of Albany in the Great Southern region of Western Australia. The suburb is bounded by the Princess Royal Harbour to the south and King George Sound to the east and is home to the Port of Albany. To the south of Port Albany, the Ataturk Channel, which connects Princess Royal Harbour with King George Sound, separates it from Vancouver Peninsula.","wpu":"Port Albany, Western Australia","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Hai_Ji%2C_Albany%2C_2019_%2802%29.jpg/960px-Hai_Ji%2C_Albany%2C_2019_%2802%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Memorial Park Cemetery (Albany, Western Australia)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.0178,"lo":117.8894,"d":1134,"ds":"Memorial Park Cemetery also known as Pioneer Cemetery and Old Albany Cemetery is a cemetery located along Middleton Road in the city of Albany in the Great Southern region of Western Australia. It was constructed in 1836 and is the first consecrated cemetery in Western Australia, gazetted in 1840 as a public burial ground to provide for the needs of a growing community.","wpu":"Memorial Park Cemetery (Albany, Western Australia)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Memorial_Cemetery1.JPG/960px-Memorial_Cemetery1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Snake Run","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.0195,"lo":117.897861,"d":1242,"ds":"The Snake Run, also known as the Albany Snake Run, Albany Skate Track and Hare Street Skate Park, is a skatepark in Albany, Western Australia. The park is the oldest community funded skatepark in Australia and the second oldest in the world. The impetus for a dedicated skatepark came following the death of a skateboarder in Albany's main street in the mid-1970s.","wpu":"Snake Run","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/WA_Albany_Snake_Run_Drone_2023.jpg/960px-WA_Albany_Snake_Run_Drone_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Port of Albany","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.036667,"lo":117.900833,"d":1445,"ds":"The Port of Albany is located within Princess Royal Harbour in King George Sound on the south coast of Western Australia, in the Great Southern region.","wpu":"Port of Albany","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Port_of_Albany.jpg/960px-Port_of_Albany.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Eyre Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.0246,"lo":117.9101,"d":1958,"ds":"The Eyre Park is a park in Middleton Beach in Albany in the Great Southern region of Western Australia. The park is bounded by Adelaide Crescent, Middleton Road and Garden Street. It has large open spaces, lakes, gazebos, barbeques, public toilets, children's play area and a basketball court.","wpu":"Eyre Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Eyre_Park_3.jpg/960px-Eyre_Park_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Princess Royal Fortress","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.030722,"lo":117.91125,"d":2048,"ds":"Princess Royal Fortress, also known as Albany Forts, was a fortress on the northern shore of Atatürk entrance on Princess Royal Harbour on Mount Adelaide overlooking King George Sound in Albany, Western Australia. It now operates as a museum.","wpu":"Princess Royal Fortress","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/PRINCESS_ROYAL_FORT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Middleton Beach, Western Australia","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.023611,"lo":117.913611,"d":2293,"ds":"Middleton Beach is a coastal suburb of Albany, Western Australia, located within the City of Albany approximately 4 kilometres (2.5 mi) east of the city centre. The traditional owners, the Noongar peoples, know the place as Binalup meaning the place of first light since the sun rises over the waters in the morning. The main road between the city and the locality is via Middleton Road.","wpu":"Middleton Beach, Western Australia","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Middleton_Beach%2C_2018_%2804%29.jpg/960px-Middleton_Beach%2C_2018_%2804%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Ellen Cove Jetty","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-35.02574,"lo":117.9172,"d":2580,"ds":"Ellen Cove Jetty also known as Middleton Beach Jetty is a jetty found at the southern end of Middleton Beach in King George Sound in Albany in the Great Southern region of Western Australia. Work commenced on the jetty with piles being driven into the sand bed at Ellen Cove in late 1899; construction was completed in 1901, at a cost of £150. The jetty served in the transport of goods and people of Albany.","wpu":"Ellen Cove Jetty","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Ellencove.JPG/960px-Ellencove.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Albany ( AL-bən-ee; Menang Noongar: Kinjarling) is a port city in the Great Southern region in the Australian state of Western Australia, 418 kilometres (260 mi) southeast of Perth, the state capital. The city centre is at the northern edge of Princess Royal Harbour, which is a part of King George Sound. The central business district is bounded by Mount Clarence to the east and Mount Melville to the west.","wpu":"Albany, Western Australia","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Consul_General_Gainer_visits_Albany%2C_WA_August_2020_%2850303439758%29.jpg/960px-Consul_General_Gainer_visits_Albany%2C_WA_August_2020_%2850303439758%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}